# --- CN memory/KB (N6): self-hosted runtime memory library ----------------------------
# Rendered by app.templates.memory_support.render_memory_source() into every generated
# Strands agent (and grafted by the self-built Harness template). Short-term memory is
# Strands' own S3SessionManager under the Launchpad snapshot prefix (ruling R5); every
# turn also lands as one AgentCore-shaped event + one SQS extraction message
# (LaunchpadMemoryHook); long-term recall is k-NN over this environment's memory index
# (`launchpad-memory`, or `launchpad-<env>-memory` — D17). Everything is env-driven
# (LAUNCHPAD_MEMORY_*, LAUNCHPAD_ENV_NAME) and fail-soft: without
# LAUNCHPAD_MEMORY_ID every entry point is a no-op, and no AWS error ever aborts a turn.
# Depends on the model block defined earlier in this file — _resolve_bedrock_api_key(),
# MODEL_REGION, BEDROCK_BEARER_ENV — because the Titan embedder authenticates with the
# agent's own Global Bedrock API key (ruling R1), never a second credential.
# Contract: docs/cn/interfaces/memory-runtime.md.
